-- title:
--   Monodromy at the cusp: a ±transvection on E[M]
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, and let $M$ be a nonzero natural number whose image in $K$ is nonzero. Let $k$ and $\Omega$ be fields, both $K$-algebras, with $\Omega$ a $k$-algebra compatibly with the $K$-structures, and with $\Omega$ an algebraic closure of $k$. Let $E$ be a Weierstrass curve over $k$ which is elliptic, and suppose that its $j$-invariant $E.j$ is transcendental over $K$ and that the $K$-subfield of $k$ generated by $E.j$ is all of $k$ (so $k$ is a rational function field $K(j)$ and $E$ has generic $j$-invariant). The assertion is the existence of two points $P_1,P_2$ on the affine model of the base change of $E$ to $\Omega$, of an algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $\Omega$ over $k$, and of an integer $\varepsilon$, such that $M\cdot P_1 = 0$, $M\cdot P_2 = 0$; for all integers $a,b$, the relation $a\cdot P_1 + b\cdot P_2 = 0$ forces $M \mid a$ and $M \mid b$ (so $P_1,P_2$ form a basis of the $M$-torsion); $\varepsilon = 1$ or $\varepsilon = -1$; and, for the action of $\sigma$ on points induced by the $k$-algebra map $\sigma \colon \Omega \to \Omega$, one has $\sigma(P_1) = \varepsilon\cdot P_1$ and $\sigma(P_2) = \varepsilon\cdot(P_1 + P_2)$.
--
--   This is the local contribution of the cusp $j = \infty$ in Igusa's determination of the Galois action on the $M$-torsion of the elliptic curve with generic $j$-invariant: the image of $\mathrm{Aut}(\Omega/k)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/M)$ contains, up to sign, a transvection, obtained by transporting the Tate curve over the Laurent series field, on which the relevant automorphism acts by the $q$-twist. It is used in the derivation of the statements that a suitable automorphism fixes a point of given order and that the action is by prescribed integral combinations of a torsion basis.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_algEquiv_map_eq_smul_and_map_eq_smul_add_of_transcendental_j.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open WeierstrassCurve WeierstrassCurve.Affine

universe u v in

theorem WeierstrassCurve.exists_algEquiv_map_eq_smul_and_map_eq_smul_add_of_transcendental_j
    (K : Type u) [Field K] [IsAlgClosed K] (M : ℕ) [NeZero M] (hM : (M : K) ≠ 0)
    (k Ω : Type v) [Field k] [Field Ω] [DecidableEq Ω] [Algebra K k] [Algebra K Ω] [Algebra k Ω]
    [IsScalarTower K k Ω] [IsAlgClosure k Ω] (E : WeierstrassCurve k) [E.IsElliptic]
    (hE : Transcendental K E.j) (hgen : IntermediateField.adjoin K ({E.j} : Set k) = ⊤) :
    ∃ (P₁ P₂ : (E.baseChange Ω).toAffine.Point) (σ : Ω ≃ₐ[k] Ω) (ε : ℤ),
      M • P₁ = 0 ∧ M • P₂ = 0 ∧
      (∀ a b : ℤ, a • P₁ + b • P₂ = 0 → (M : ℤ) ∣ a ∧ (M : ℤ) ∣ b) ∧
      (ε = 1 ∨ ε = -1) ∧
      WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point.map (σ : Ω →ₐ[k] Ω) P₁ = ε • P₁ ∧
      WeierstrassCurve.Affine.Point.map (σ : Ω →ₐ[k] Ω) P₂ = ε • (P₁ + P₂) := by sorry
